This port reuses upstream source logic, strings, resources and artwork. All of it
remains under that MIT License. Modifications made for the HarmonyOS platform are
released under the same terms.

This port is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by Ranchero Software
or Brent Simmons. Please do not report problems with this port to the upstream
project. The names "NetNewsWire" and "Ranchero Software" and the NetNewsWire app
icon belong to their respective owners; the MIT License covers the source code,
not those names or that artwork.


Bundled third-party assets
--------------------------

Article themes under entry/src/main/resources/rawfile/themes/ are carried over
from upstream NetNewsWire and embed the following fonts:

* Atkinson Hyperlegible (Hyperlegible.nnwtheme)
  Copyright (c) 2020 Braille Institute of America, Inc.
  Licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1.
  https://www.brailleinstitute.org/freefont
  https://openfontlicense.org/

* ModeSeven (NewsFax.nnwtheme)
  Freeware, with additional edits by schriftgestalt.
  See entry/src/main/resources/rawfile/themes/NewsFax.nnwtheme/License.md
  https://www.fontspace.com/modeseven-font-f2369

Article rendering scripts under entry/src/main/resources/rawfile/article/ are
carried over from upstream NetNewsWire. newsfoot.js is by Andrew Brehaut.

In-app credits for upstream contributors ship in
entry/src/main/resources/rawfile/about/credits.txt and are shown on the About
screen.
